; AmiBroker ASCII import format for the Banyu Langit export.
;
; WHERE THIS GOES:  C:\Program Files\AmiBroker\Formats\  (next to the other .format files)
; File name matters: this one is "banyulangit.format" only as a label — AmiBroker picks the
; format by the DATA file's extension (.csv). If you already have a .csv format defined, either
; merge these lines into it or rename the exported files to .blk / .txt and name this format to
; match. Do not let two different .csv formats compete for the same extension.
;
; The column order here MUST match server/scripts/export-amibroker.js:
;   Ticker,YYYY-MM-DD,Open,High,Low,Close,Volume

$FORMAT Ticker,Date_YMD,Open,High,Low,Close,Volume
$SEPARATOR ,
$AUTOADD 1
$OVERWRITE 1
$SKIPLINES 0
$DEBUG 1
